# Trust-root paths: what the owner reads on every change (ADR-0023, ADR-0030, ADR-0033).
# Listing them here does nothing by itself. "Require review from Code Owners" in the
# protect-main ruleset is the owner's change, made by hand; once it is on, a pull request that
# touches a path below needs @s0fractal's approval, which GitHub never takes from the pull
# request's own author. The last matching line wins.
.github/witness-signers             @s0fractal
scripts/witness-pin.py              @s0fractal
.github/workflows/witness-gate.yml  @s0fractal
docs/witness-manifest.json          @s0fractal
docs/witness-manifest.json.sig      @s0fractal
docs/adr/                           @s0fractal
.github/CODEOWNERS                  @s0fractal
# Who may accept contracts and pull requests (roles) and whose keys count (trust), ADR-0033.
.warrant/v3.json                    @s0fractal
.warrant/merge.json                 @s0fractal
